# TypeScript Project Rules

## Testing
- ALWAYS run tests after generating or modifying code
- Use Vitest for unit tests: `npm run test`
- Run tests in watch mode during development: `npm run test:watch`
- Minimum 80% coverage for new code
- Tests must pass before committing
- Colocate tests with source code in `__tests__/` folders or use `.test.ts` suffix

## Package Management
- Use npm ONLY (never yarn or pnpm)
- Always commit package-lock.json
- Run `npm install` after package.json changes
- Check for vulnerabilities: `npm audit`

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Follow ESLint rules: `npm run lint`
- Format with Prettier: `npm run format`
- Run type checking: `npm run typecheck`
- All quality checks must pass before committing

## TypeScript Best Practices
- Use explicit types for function parameters and return values
- Prefer interfaces over type aliases for object shapes
- Use `unknown` instead of `any` when type is truly unknown
- Enable strict null checks
- Use const assertions for literal types
- Prefer `readonly` for immutable data

## Module System
- Use ES modules (import/export)
- No CommonJS (require/module.exports) in new code
- Use named exports for utilities
- Use default export for main class/function
- Organize imports: external, internal, types

## Error Handling
- Use custom error classes for domain errors
- Include error context (userId, requestId, etc.)
- Log errors with structured logging
- Return explicit error types (Result<T, E> pattern)
- Never swallow errors silently

## Async/Await
- Prefer async/await over raw promises
- Always handle promise rejections
- Use try/catch for error handling
- Set timeouts for external calls
- Use Promise.all for parallel operations

## Documentation
- Add JSDoc for all public APIs
- Include examples in JSDoc
- Update README.md for user-facing changes
- Document complex algorithms
- Explain non-obvious decisions

## Security
- Never commit secrets or API keys
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Validate all user inputs
- Sanitize data before logging
- Use parameterized queries for databases

## Performance
- Avoid unnecessary allocations in hot paths
- Use streaming for large data
- Implement caching where appropriate
- Profile before optimizing
- Set timeouts for external calls

## Git Commits
- Follow conventional commits format
- Reference Linear/Jira issue in commit body
- Keep commits focused and atomic
- Write clear commit messages

## Project-Specific Conventions
- Entry point: `src/index.ts`
- Build output: `dist/`
- Test files: `src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts`
- Types: `src/types/`

## Quality Checklist Before PR
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Coverage meets threshold (80%)
- [ ] Linting passes
- [ ] Type checking passes
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No console.log or debugging code
- [ ] No TODOs without linked issues
